have you seen https://forum.astralinux.ru/threads/3415/ ?
maybe you version of Astra Linux Orel contain errors....

@jurim76 
1. postgres authentificate auth_query_user with trust auth-method:
https://github.com/yandex/odyssey/blob/303fbaa73000dfdfc306083e9c81bd83d93d5fbe/docker/bin/setup#L28
password cannot be used for auth_query_user authentication

2. insert first line in your hba.conf (172.16.0.0/24 - its only for example, here must be ip of odyssey ):
host    all             auth_query_user            172.16.0.0/24         trust
execute on postgresql server:
SELECT pg_reload_conf();
CREATE USER "auth_query_user" WITH password 'test_pass';
ALTER  USER "auth_query_user" with superuser;
on the odyssey host try connect to postgres:
$ psql -h 172.16.0.235 -d postgres --user=auth_query_user
$ postgres=# SELECT usename, passwd FROM pg_shadow;

3. Perhaps you did not configure postgresql for host based auth-method

Defining database "postgres" with internal routing works for me

`    storage "testdb" {
      type "remote"
      host "testdb"
      port 5432
    }

    database "postgres" {
      user "pgbouncer" {
        authentication "none"
        pool_routing "internal"
        storage "testdb"
        pool "session"
      }
    }

    database "test" {
      user default {
        authentication "md5"
        auth_query "SELECT uname,phash FROM pgbouncer.user_lookup($1)"
        auth_query_user "pgbouncer"
        auth_query_db "postgres"
        storage "testdb"
        ...
      }
   }    
`

I am also encountering this error.

I can see this issue is labelled as a `bug`. Any idea if we can expect the fix soon? 

@jayant07-yb Have you been able to to find a workaround for this? We are also using yugabyte as the storage.
